      "problem": "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a\\in Z,$ if $15∣6a,$ then $15∣a.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nLet's choose $a=$ {{field-6}}.\nThen, we have that \n\n$$\n15{{field-7}}{{30}_{⏟}}_{6a}\\,\\text{and}\\,15{{field-8}}{{5}_{⏟}}_{a}.\n$$\n\nSo, $a=$ {{field-9}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false.",
